---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { DISCORD } from '../data/site.js';
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy | StainBoost" heading="Privacy policy" path="/privacy" updated="September 2026"
  description="What personal data StainBoost collects, why, how long it is kept, and how to ask for it to be deleted.">
  <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account:</strong> if you sign up with email — your email, username and password (stored only as a secure hash). If you sign in with Discord — your Discord ID and username.</li>
    <li><strong>Orders:</strong> what you order (ranks or wins, queue, LP info, extras, Flash key, server), your Discord username and League Riot ID, the order total, and order progress.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> what you write in the chat on your order page.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments:</strong> only that you told us you paid and with which method. Payments happen on PayPal or Binance — we never see or store card, PayPal or Binance account details.</li>
    <li><strong>Referrals:</strong> your referral code, who referred you, and your credit balance.</li>
    <li><strong>Waitlist:</strong> the Discord username or email you give us if you ask to be told when EUW/EUNE opens.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical:</strong> your IP address, used only to limit abuse (rate limiting).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your League account password is <strong>never entered on this website</strong>. For a solo boost it is exchanged with Stain directly, used only to log in and play, and not kept afterwards. You can change it when the boost is done.</p>

  <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To take, play and track your order, and to contact you about it.</li>
    <li>To run the referral program and apply credit.</li>
    <li>To tell you when EUW/EUNE opens — only if you asked.</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Chat assistant</h2>
  <p>Messages you type into the "Ask a question" chat are sent to our AI provider (Groq) to generate a reply. Please don't share personal details there.</p>

  <h2>4. Where it's stored</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Vercel. Account and order data is stored in an Upstash Redis database (through Vercel) and encrypted in transit. Sign-in uses a secure, HTTP-only cookie.</p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Orders and order chats: deleted automatically 90 days after the order is placed.</li>
    <li>Accounts, referral codes and credit: kept until you ask us to delete them.</li>
    <li>Reviews: public until you ask us to remove yours.</li>
    <li>Waitlist: until the server opens or you ask to be removed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Other services we use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> how visitors use the site (pages, clicks, orders placed).</li>
    <li><strong>Vercel Analytics &amp; Speed Insights:</strong> anonymous visit and performance statistics.</li>
    <li><strong>Discord:</strong> sign-in and communication with Stain.</li>
    <li><strong>Groq:</strong> the AI chat assistant.</li>
    <li><strong>PayPal and Binance:</strong> payments, under their own privacy policies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A sign-in cookie that keeps you logged in (needed for your dashboard and orders).</li>
    <li>Google Analytics cookies.</li>
    <li>Your browser's local storage, to keep your order while you sign in, remember a referral code for 30 days, and show your sign-in status without flicker.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. We don't sell your data</h2>
  <p>We never sell, trade or rent your personal data.</p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask for a copy of your data or for it to be deleted at any time — message <strong>{DISCORD.handle}</strong> on Discord.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>StainBoost is not intended for anyone under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The latest version is always on this page with its date.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Message <strong>{DISCORD.handle}</strong> on Discord.</p>
</LegalPage>
